    "description": "The hardest part of repainting a white ceiling is seeing where you have already painted. KILZ Color Change Ceiling Paint solves that by going on with a visible tint and drying to white, so each roller pass is easy to track while wet. That makes missed patches, thin coverage and uneven overlaps obvious before the paint dries, which helps beginners get an even coat and lets experienced painters move faster without second-guessing. Once dry, it is a flat white that hides minor flaws. The color change depends on drying, so in cool or humid rooms it can take longer to shift, and you should wait for the full change before judging the final result. It offers fewer options than conventional ceiling paints, as it is designed to dry white. For anyone repainting white over white, especially in large or brightly lit rooms, it is a clever tool, and owner feedback consistently mentions how much easier it makes coverage to judge."
