          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I paint a popcorn ceiling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Test for asbestos first if the home was built before the 1980s. If the texture is safe and intact, use a thick-nap roller with light pressure or spray with a paint sprayer to avoid loosening the texture. Do not overwork the surface, and plan for more paint than a smooth ceiling, since texture absorbs more."
          }
        }
