          </p>

          <p>
            Add roughly $30 to $70 for roller covers, a roller frame, an extension pole, an angled brush, drop cloths, painter's tape and stain-blocking primer. Professional ceiling painting typically costs more per square foot than walls because of the extra setup and difficulty, often a few hundred dollars per room depending on region, ceiling height and condition.
          </p>

          <p>
            Buy all the paint you need at once and box it, mixing cans together in a large bucket so the color and sheen are consistent across the whole ceiling. Keep a small amount of leftover paint labeled with the room and date for touch-ups, which blend best when done with the original batch.
